This project develops a machine learning framework for automatically identifying financial market regimes from historical price and volume data. 
The objective is to classify daily market conditions into four economically meaningful states:
•	Bull Market
•	Bear Market
•	Sideways Market
•	High-Volatility Market
Rather than relying solely on price trends, the framework combines probabilistic unsupervised learning with supervised machine learning to characterize 
evolving market dynamics. The resulting regime classifications are incorporated into a confidence-weighted trading strategy whose performance is evaluated against 
a passive buy-and-hold benchmark.
